# Task 3 fix 2: lifecycle of ~/.local/share/onlyoffice/desktopeditors/data/recover/ (iso5-dcli, 2026-11-12 19:10-19:15)
Each open document gets a dir DE__xxxxxx/ with a full copy of the file, Editor.bin (~440 KB), asc_name.info, user_name.log
(and changes/changes0.json once edited). Home is mode 700; the dirs inside are 755.
A. clean close of the tab, "No" to "save the changes?" (docx open, unsaved edit): recover/ = 0 files right after (app stays running on its start page). EMPTIED.
   (ctrl+q did nothing in the Xvfb session; the tab close button was used.)
B. kill -9 of DesktopEditors + editors_helper with an unsaved edit: recover/ = 5 files (copy + Editor.bin + changes0.json containing the edit). KEPT.
   Next launch shows a "Recover" list with the document; the copy stays until the user acts on it (no timeout seen).
   (Added in Task 9) "No timeout seen" = ~5 min, inside the 19:10-19:15 window in the header line; the start and end of this observation itself were not recorded.
C. logout: session 454 scope (app started with setsid in that ssh session): `loginctl terminate-session` did not stop the app (KillUserProcesses is the default `no`), copy kept;
   then `systemctl kill --signal=SIGKILL session-454.scope`: app gone, recover/ = 4 files (copy + Editor.bin...). KEPT.
Also kept indefinitely: recents.xml (full paths of every file opened) and the Chromium cache/profile.
Cleaned up after the test (recover/, test copies removed).
